---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/usgaap/asc720.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — a Residual Expense Topic" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Start-Up Costs (720-15)" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Advertising Costs" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Restructuring Costs" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — Start-Up Cost Expense Recognition" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Advertising Cost Periods" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s10", label: "ASC 720 vs IFRS — Dissimilar Comparison" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Related Topics" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A catch-all for miscellaneous operating expenses</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 720 is explicitly a residual Topic — it governs expenses that are NOT adequately addressed by other, more specific Topics in the Codification. Because it covers diverse expense types without a unifying theme, its guidance on recognition and measurement is often tied to the specific economic substance of each expense type rather than a single overarching principle.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — a Residual Expense Topic</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Start-up costs, advertising, restructuring</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 720 covers start-up costs (720-15), advertising costs, restructuring costs, and other miscellaneous operating expenses. It does NOT cover compensation costs (ASC 710/712/715/718), cost of sales (ASC 705), or income taxes (ASC 740). Each subtopic addresses a different expense type with recognition rules tailored to that type's specific economics.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Start-Up Costs (720-15)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Expensed as incurred</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">Start-up costs — costs incurred during the organisation and pre-operating phase of a new entity or operation — must be EXPENSED as incurred under ASC 720-15. This includes costs such as legal and accounting fees, promotional expenses, and training costs incurred before the entity begins normal operations. Capitalisation is NOT permitted.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Advertising Costs</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Generally expensed when the advertising takes place</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">Advertising costs are generally EXPENSED when the advertising takes place — when the advertising activity occurs or when the advertising message is first communicated. Costs for direct-response advertising MAY be capitalised and amortised if they meet the criteria in ASC 340-20, but ordinary brand advertising is expensed as incurred.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Restructuring Costs</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Expensed when incurred, not when announced</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">Restructuring costs are EXPENSED when the entity INCURS the cost, not when the restructuring is announced or planned. This means termination benefits are recognised when employees are notified and the amounts can be estimated, lease termination costs are recognised when the entity terminates the lease, and other restructuring costs are recognised as the related services are received.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Worked Example — Start-Up Cost Expense Recognition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Pre-operating costs of a new restaurant</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Pre-opening restaurant costs</div><div class="wk-body">A restaurant entity incurs $180,000 during its pre-opening phase: $80,000 in employee training costs, $50,000 in grand-opening advertising, and $50,000 in legal/accounting fees to set up the entity.</div><div class="wk-answer">ALL three cost types are EXPENSED as incurred under ASC 720: Training costs ($80,000) + Advertising ($50,000) + Legal/accounting ($50,000) = <strong>$180,000</strong> recognised as start-up/organisation expense in the period incurred — none are capitalised as an asset.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Advertising Cost Periods</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">When advertising costs hit expense</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Television advertising campaign</div><div class="wk-body">An entity pays $120,000 in November for television advertising spots that will air in January, February, and March of the following year.</div><div class="wk-answer">Under ASC 720, the $120,000 is EXPENSED when the advertising takes place — that is, in January, February, and March when the ads actually air — NOT in November when the payment was made. The prepayment creates a deferred asset (prepaid expense) until the air dates.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASC 720 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and amount of significant advertising and promotional costs</span><span>Significant restructuring costs, including the nature of the restructuring and its expected completion date</span><span>Period costs included in cost of sales, if any</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Critical Judgments & Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
      <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether direct-response advertising meets the criteria for capitalisation under ASC 340-20</span><span>When restructuring costs are incurred versus merely announced</span></div></div>
      <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Amount of restructuring costs that can be reliably estimated at the announcement date</span><span>Expected completion date and timing of restructuring-related cash flows</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>ASC 720 vs IFRS — Dissimilar Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASC 720 vs IFRS</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">US GAAP (ASC 720)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Start-up costs</span><span>Expensed as incurred</span><span>Expensed as incurred</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Advertising</span><span>Expensed when the advertising takes place</span><span>Similar treatment — expensed when received</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Restructuring</span><span>Expensed when costs are incurred</span><span>IAS 37 requires recognition when a constructive obligation arises</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">Restructuring represents the most divergence between ASC 720 and IFRS — IAS 37's constructive obligation concept often requires earlier recognition than US GAAP's incurred-cost model.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every ASC 720 event lands</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Start-up costs</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Expensed as incurred</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Advertising costs</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Expensed when the advertising takes place</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Restructuring costs</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Expensed when incurred, not when announced</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Related Topics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Topic</span><span>Connection</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 340</span><span>Other Assets and Deferred Costs — governs capitalised advertising (direct-response)</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 420</span><span>Exit or Disposal Cost Obligations — governs one-time termination benefits</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>IAS 37</span><span>Provisions, Contingent Liabilities and Contingent Assets — IFRS restructuring equivalent</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.ASC720 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>

